1
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:16,310
Good morning, Susan.

2
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:22,960
Good morning, Sam.

3
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:27,320
What's the schedule today?

4
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:28,150
Ten o'clock,

5
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:30,480
telephone FAO Schwarz about the new twin baby dolls.

6
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:31,680
OK.

7
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:35,410
Telephone Mrs. Zaskey at the advertising agency.

8
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:36,550
I did that. Go on.

9
00:00:36,550 --> 00:00:39,070
Eleven o'clock, approve the sketches for the toy spaceship.

10
00:00:39,070 --> 00:00:40,120
Where are they?

11
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:41,680
Right here.

12
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:43,410
Did you look at them?

13
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:45,460
Yes, I did.

14
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,700
What do you think of the spaceship?

15
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:49,750
I think the kids'll love it.

16
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:56,080
Would you show me the drawings, please?

17
00:00:56,080 --> 00:01:01,310
Huh.

18
00:01:01,310 --> 00:01:04,140
Now, what else is on the schedule today?

19
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:05,680
Well, at one o'clock

20
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:07,710
you have a lunch appointment with Mr. Levine,

21
00:01:07,710 --> 00:01:09,640
the client from the Toytown Stores.

22
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:10,940
Where?

23
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:12,400
At Rossano's.

24
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,890
Hmm. Anything else?

25
00:01:14,890 --> 00:01:15,860
At four o'clock,

26
00:01:15,860 --> 00:01:17,220
you have a meeting with the production staff

27
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:18,500
in the conference room.

28
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:21,050
Make sure everybody is at that meeting.

29
00:01:21,050 --> 00:01:22,310
Will do.

30
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:25,190
At six you're meeting, Mr. Ozawa.

31
00:01:25,190 --> 00:01:27,430
Oh, yes. Are his models here?

32
00:01:27,430 --> 00:01:28,360
They're in my office.

33
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:29,130
I'd like to see them.

34
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,600
Right.

35
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:36,850
What else?

36
00:01:36,850 --> 00:01:39,240
Come on, Sam ...

37
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:42,110
You work too hard, Susan.

38
00:01:42,110 --> 00:01:44,580
When was your last day off?

39
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:47,070
Hmm. I can't remember.

40
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:49,580
You really ought to take some time off.

41
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:50,670
What for?

42
00:01:50,670 --> 00:01:54,270
To enjoy the simple things in life ...

43
00:01:54,270 --> 00:01:56,420
I know, Sam.

44
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:58,270
Maybe soon.

45
00:01:58,270 --> 00:02:00,850
To smell the flowers.

46
00:02:00,850 --> 00:02:04,490
Oh, wait a minute. What's today's date?

47
00:02:04,490 --> 00:02:06,950
Today is the twelfth. Why?

48
00:02:06,950 --> 00:02:14,210
It seems to me I scheduled something else.

49
00:02:14,210 --> 00:02:17,060
There's nothing else in the appointment book.

50
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:19,100
I'm sure I did.

51
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:23,010
Oh, well, I'll probably remember it later.

52
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:24,490
I hope it isn't important.

53
00:02:24,490 --> 00:02:26,600
Hmm. It's probably nothing.

54
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,420
OK, let's get started.

55
00:02:28,420 --> 00:02:31,850
Would you call Priscilla Smith at FAO Schwarz, please?

56
00:02:31,850 --> 00:02:39,420
Right.

57
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:41,880
These are the models from the Japanese film maker.

58
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:46,820
Thank you. Just put them on my desk.

59
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:51,380
And the new drawings for the toy spaceship.

60
00:02:51,380 --> 00:03:01,260
Wonderful.

61
00:03:01,260 --> 00:03:02,760
That was fast.

62
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:03,830
We have a new artist.

63
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:05,360
She's very talented.

64
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,710
What time is it, anyway?

65
00:03:06,710 --> 00:03:07,560
My watch stopped.

66
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:09,360
It's eleven thirty.

67
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:12,970
What time is my lunch date with Bill Levine?

68
00:03:12,970 --> 00:03:14,940
One o'clock.

69
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:18,280
Remind me to leave at twelve forty-five.

70
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:20,950
Did you remember your other appointment for today?

71
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:22,590
No,

72
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:23,890
but I have a feeling

73
00:03:23,890 --> 00:03:38,940
it's going to be too late when I do remember.

74
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:40,740
Yes, Sam?

75
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:43,810
I just solved the mystery.

76
00:03:43,810 --> 00:03:45,050
What did I forget?

77
00:03:45,050 --> 00:03:48,010
You have some guests in the reception room.

78
00:03:48,010 --> 00:03:49,910
What? Who?

79
00:03:49,910 --> 00:03:52,890
Mr. Harry Bennett and his daughter.

80
00:03:52,890 --> 00:03:54,530
I remember!

81
00:03:54,530 --> 00:03:57,100
Oh ... Harry!

82
00:03:57,100 --> 00:04:00,770
I made a lunch date with him and his daughter weeks ago.

83
00:04:00,770 --> 00:04:04,750
Is he a client?

84
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:07,710
He's a friend.

85
00:04:07,710 --> 00:04:11,310
Well, he's here with his daughter to have lunch.

86
00:04:11,310 --> 00:04:12,790
I met her at Thanksgiving,

87
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:17,040
and I promised to have lunch with both of them today.

88
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,810
Yes, indeed.

89
00:04:18,810 --> 00:04:20,940
What are you going to do about your appointment

90
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:24,530
with Mr. Levine?

91
00:04:24,530 --> 00:04:29,430
Any suggestions?

92
00:04:29,430 --> 00:04:32,430
Oh!
